digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56857-z
  rankdir="TB";
  "I1" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: SLE involves genes but factors are hard to find."];
  "I10" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: NCF1 R90H links Low ROS to SLE risk."];
  "I12" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-reasoning: Ncf1 mutation causes lupus via interferon."];
  "I14" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: MNV is a candidate environmental trigger."];
  "I16" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Viral infections are plausible autoimmune triggers."];
  "I4" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: Animal models can identify SLE genes."];
  "I8" [label="(0,0,0) Abduction-reasoning: Human NCF1 has functional R90H variant."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes that the lupus-risk Ncf1/NCF1 R90H polymorphism reduces ROS production and creates genetic susceptibility to systemic lupus erythematosus, but severe disease in mice emerges specifically when that susceptibility is paired with murine norovirus infection rather than pristane/SPF conditions alone, thereby testing a gene-environment synergy between NCF1 variation and viral infection.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A genetic lupus-risk variant that lowers ROS may require an environmental infectious exposure to reveal severe autoimmune disease, so comparing pathogen-free or pristane-only conditions with murine norovirus exposure can identify gene-environment synergy."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Human NCF1 R90H is a functional NCF1 variant linked with decreased ROS response and SLE risk."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Because Ncf1-mutant lupus is associated with interferon signaling and MNV is a possible environmental factor relevant to interferon activation, MNV is a candidate factor to test in Ncf1 lupus."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) Viral infections, including MNV as a candidate factor, are plausible triggers to investigate in Ncf1-associated lupus."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) Environmental stimulation can be relevant to the expression of genetic autoimmune risk and NCF1-regulated immune differences."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) Viral infection is a plausible environmental trigger to test in genetically susceptible Ncf1-associated lupus."];
  "R20" [label="(0,0,0) MNV infection is a demonstrated trigger, though not necessarily the only possible trigger, for severe lupus development in Ncf1 90H mice."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) In Ncf1 90H mice, MNV infection can precipitate severe lupus when genetic susceptibility is present."];
  "R22" [label="(0,0,0) The contrast between no enhanced lupus under SPF conditions and severe lupus after MNV infection supports a gene-environment interaction between Ncf1 90H and viral exposure."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) SLE research involves difficult-to-pinpoint genetic factors together with environmental-factor interplay."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Animal models are one available approach for identifying SLE-related genes in the context of complex genetic and environmental contributions."];
  "S10_VP1" [label="(10,1,0) Known that SNP NCF1 R90H replaces arginine with histidine."];
  "S11_VP1" [label="(11,1,0) Observed high odds ratio for NCF1-339 in SLE cohorts."];
  "S12_VP1" [label="(12,1,0) Observed NCF1 90H allele caused decreased ROS response."];
  "S13_VP3" [label="(13,3,0) Observed BALB/c mice with Ncf1 m1J developed severe pristane-induced lupus."];
  "S14_VP1" [label="(14,1,0) Known that Ncf1 m1J mutation was associated with activation of interferon signaling."];
  "S15_VP1" [label="(15,1,0) Currently an important question remains why interferon response is triggered."];
  "S16_VP2" [label="(16,2,0) If MNV antibodies detected, then norovirus is a possible environmental factor."];
  "S17_VP3" [label="(17,3,0) Observed DNA viruses suggested to have disease association."];
  "S19_VP1" [label="(19,1,0) Observed Covid-19 triggers autoimmune diseases in predisposed patients."];
  "S1_VP3" [label="(1,3,0) If SLE involves unknown genes, then genetic factors contribute to SLE."];
  "S1_VP4" [label="(1,4,0) Currently there is an interplay of environmental factors in SLE."];
  "S20_VP1" [label="(20,1,0) If genetic predisposition accounts for risk, then interacting environmental factors are needed."];
  "S21_VP2" [label="(21,2,0) Currently NCF1-regulated differences seen only after immunization."];
  "S25_VP1" [label="(25,1,0) Observed Ncf1 90H allele does not enhance lupus in SPF conditions."];
  "S26_VP1" [label="(26,1,0) Known that infection with MNV causes development of severe lupus in Ncf1 90H mice."];
  "S2_VP1" [label="(2,1,0) Observed difficulty in pinpointing causative factors of SLE."];
  "S5_VP1" [label="(5,1,0) If genetic crosses of inbred animals are used, then underlying genes can be identified."];
  "S6_VP2" [label="(6,2,0) Currently studies in mice and rats identified important SNPs."];
  "S9_VP2" [label="(9,2,0) Observed functionally important SNP identified in human NCF1."];
